div.p:
Mr. Kissinger: That’s no longer feasible;
                    it had to do with getting Sirik Matak into
                    the government.

Mr. Porter: But South Vietnam has some
                    responsibility for its own defense. We don’t know what we may get in Cambodia;
                    we may even get Sihanouk back again.

note.p:
Source: National Archives, Nixon
                    Presidential Materials, NSC Files, NSC Institutional Files (H–Files), Box H–117, WSAG Meeting Minutes, Originals, 1973. Top Secret;
                    Sensitive. The meeting was held in the White House Situation Room.
